GTNH-SmallAddons

Small GTNH addons.

build --> ./gradlew build

Linked Input Hatch
shared --> 4 x 64,000 L tanks by channel
private --> owner-only channel
circuit --> local per hatch
data stick --> left-click copy / right-click paste
screwdriver --> filter / sneak sorting

CRIB Wildcard Patterns
pattern --> same-material GregTech inputs/outputs expand across valid unifiable materials
toggle --> wildcard button or sneak + right-click Soft Mallet

AE2 Interface Wildcard Patterns
pattern --> same wildcard expansion for AE2 Interfaces
toggle --> left-side button in the AE2 item-pattern Interface GUI, or sneak + right-click Soft Mallet
applies --> full-block and cable-part Interfaces, including AE2FC Dual Interfaces

CRIB Non-Consumable Inputs
NC --> reserved reusable processing-pattern catalyst
mark --> shift + right-click pattern input
requires --> NC item in ME storage
result --> reserved once, not consumed, returned after craft
wildcard + NC --> supported

XTProfile
location --> automatic inside the AE2 Crafting CPU window
CPU --> per-crafting-CPU Interface / CRIB / machine routes
All --> complete server-session view
Time --> AE2 processing dispatch until expected output returns
parallel --> overlapping route operations are not double-counted
TPS --> separate GregTech machine tick-cost sampling
search --> Interface / CRIB / machine names

Configuration
file --> config/xt9yfeatures.cfg (generated on first launch)
[features] --> each switch defaults to true; restart game/server after changes
linkedInputHatch --> Linked Input Hatch registration and recipe
cribWildcard --> CRIB wildcard expansion, button, Soft Mallet toggle
ae2InterfaceWildcard --> full-block, cable-part and AE2FC Interface wildcard features
cribNonConsumable --> non-consumable pattern inputs, reservations and NEI integration
xtProfile --> route tracking, timings and Crafting CPU side panel
betterLoadingScreenCompat --> Better Loading Screen background-refresh workaround
server/client --> keep gameplay options matching on both sides
existing worlds --> do not disable linkedInputHatch while installed hatches are present
NC reservations --> existing reserved items are still refunded if cribNonConsumable is disabled

XTProfile GUI
scale --> panel automatically fits alongside the AE2 Crafting CPU at the current Minecraft GUI scale
input --> panel buttons, search, rows and scrollbar use the scaled coordinate mapping

Virtual Extraction (GTNH)
config --> config/xt9yfeatures.cfg; generated/saved every launch, with defaults and descriptions
voidMiners --> false by default; GT single-block miners and multiblock ore drills produce the current dimension's weighted Void Miner ores without removing terrain
voidPumps --> false by default; GT fluid-block pumps leave source fluids intact; GT underground-fluid drills use pristine per-chunk yields and do not lower deposits
oreSourceBlock --> true by default; registers the Virtual Ore Chunk Source even when disabled, to preserve existing block IDs
block recipe --> I R I / R D R / I R I (I: iron block, R: redstone, D: diamond block)
placement --> PersonalSpace worlds only, at most one source per chunk
right-click --> next dimension; sneak + right-click --> previous dimension
dimensions --> dynamically enumerated from GTNH's native Void Miner pools AND all enabled ore generation layers (including planets that native Void Mining excludes): Overworld, Underdark/Deep Dark, Nether, End and registered planets
scope --> ONLY the one chunk containing the source, in the PersonalSpace dimension where the block is placed
ore outputs --> sampled using GTNH ore weights (not all ore types in every individual cycle); does not generate ore blocks in terrain
requirements --> normal machine power, progress, output limitations and multiblock drilling fluid still apply
defaults --> major gameplay changes are off until enabled explicitly; changing the config requires restart
persistence --> tile NBT in the world save is authoritative; oreSources section of config is a preload/readable mirror keyed by save name + seed + dimension ID + chunk
safety --> config entries from worlds not currently loaded are ignored; no world or chunk is created/loaded from them; remove the block to remove its entry
compatibility --> disabling oreSourceBlock disables the effect, but leaves its registered block and existing tile NBT intact
notes --> unrelated mods' independent mining/pumping implementations are not automatically intercepted
